# A region holding two panes side by side: the writing and the artifact, or a
# scroll of reading and the try-it beside it. It exists so the region has a
# name a stylesheet can hold — `box` plus a class, which is the house's tool
# for display real estate, said once here rather than in every page.
#
# It is one word for one concept across the studio. The classic UI called its
# copy `split_pane` and the workbench called this `panes` — the same region
# under two names, and a thing with two names has two homes. The name that
# survived is the one the language already knows: the design compiler
# dissolves a `panes` wrapper inside a `horizon`, so the zones reach the shell
# grid directly.
box
  children
